      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_10eb532869b3629a2f4886e074254ae81e022ec1766c6a06be94fd06d6ce2d76",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Zero terms transfer geometry into arithmetic in two complementary ways: controlling all relevant real parts bounds prime-counting error, while after smoothing and under RH, isolating a low conjugate pair and bounding the remaining tail forces both signs of oscillation. These are upper-control and lower-oscillation uses of zero expansions, not interchangeable estimates.",
