    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_153907bccc06bf289c754bf78c47cabf23ba5d1104a5d630af3d30bae2944f27",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion separates the nontrivial divisor from zeta's gamma and pole artifacts and exposes the involution s↦1−s. Pairing zeros under that involution and using a quadratic invariant then removes the pair orientation and yields a qualitatively lower-order secondary sequence; this is a symmetry quotient, not a relabeling of uncompleted zeros.",
