      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2803eff533110ca17d8186e038e373486f6f76e190d2181e51b9786a92f6747e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Small holomorphic shifts form a generating family for differentiated moments: first prove a uniform undifferentiated estimate, then use shift differential operators and Cauchy contours to extract zeta derivatives without differentiating an uncontrolled error. In multi-piece moments, apparent divided-difference poles must be converted to integral forms and symmetric contributions recombined before coincident-shift specialization.",
