    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2d57aa70ac72f94878c1a11812d0707cb94c9040a39d5b42c8e6491a432b00ef",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Conductor scaling produces unit-density family zero statistics, and splitting by functional-equation sign exposes distinct orthogonal symmetry kernels. A nonnegative band-limited one-level test converts the limiting density into bounds on central vanishing, while the parity-dependent off-diagonal prime–Kloosterman term explains where SO(even) and SO(odd) separate despite matching diagonal contributions.",
