    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_32d2931f8e6c21486c91ac89373be5f73cedea99e1e7da0a5fcd1f05555eeb26",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For analytic almost-periodic functions, vertical means of log|f| form a convex Jensen function whose slope differences encode stripwise zero frequency. Littlewood's lemma instead integrates boundary log modulus to encode a zero count or first horizontal-displacement moment. Both are log-potential projections of a divisor, but they retain different coordinates and are not equal observables.",
