    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_45c3e1ceb57facae4c69cd5e4c491e0357f1333c1b844fa037b7b47f77435e77",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Truncated Möbius inversion has two logically different effects: divisor convolution can create exact initial coefficient gaps, while mean-square, large-sieve, and contour estimates only suppress the remaining coefficients in aggregate. Variants of this algebraic-gap plus analytic-residual design support both family averages and typical shifted-line inversion.",
